    ; The SHALLOW store scan, kept for the one caller that must not change: a
    ; body's top-level statements plus one Block level, matching the shape and
    ; not what is stored. This is the answer void storers have had all along.
    function action_shallow_store(func: Function, a: Action) @ret_nonlocal true returns bool linked
































    ; Walk a body for a store into a ref PARAMETER. DEEP: every statement and
    ; every operand, so a store inside a `while`, a `choose` arm or a nested
    ; block counts. It used to walk the body's top-level statements and ONE
    ; Block level only, and the miss was silent in the one direction that is a
    ; memory fault -- no page, so a value the callee builds FOR THE CALLER lands
    ; on a frame that is released on return. The arm list below is closed (every
    ; Expression arm that can contain a statement or an operand is handled), so
    ; completeness needs no conservative fallback.
    ;
    ; `require_build` carries proc_needs_caller_page_for_storage's void/non-void
    ; split into ONE traversal, so both questions are asked of exactly the same
    ; store sites: a void storer fires on the shape alone, a non-void one must
    ; also BUILD something at the store.
    function action_stores_into_ref_param(func: Function, a: Action, require_build: bool) @ret_nonlocal true returns bool linked





